<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαλβίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῖδος</span>, ἡ, prop. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rope drawn across the race-course at the starting and
				finishing-point:</i> mostly in pl., <i>posts to which this
				rope was attached,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1159
			</span></i>: so in sg., <i>turning-post,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσος β. ξεστῇ εἴκασται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					5.5
				</span></i>
			: also, <i>platform from which the quoit was thrown,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Im.</u>
				1.24
			</span></i>: hence, <i>any starting-point,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho Soph.
				69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαλβίδων ἄπο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					867
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				548
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρπε πρὸς βαλβῖδα λυπηρὰν βίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1245
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ β. εἰς τέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					13.177d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. λόγου βέβληται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.20.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					4.3b
				</span></i>
			.<i><span class="en">
				75
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); but, <i>edge,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> since
				<i>the starting-point</i> was also <i>the goal,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαλβῖδες</span> was used for <i>any point
				to be gained,</i> as <i>the battlements</i> (by one scaling a
			wall), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				131
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				287
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.513
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιλότης παραμήκης</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.87
			</span></i>; v. foreg.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
